// Aerobee (1947).
// Aerobee sounding rocket: the XASR-1 sustainer on an Aerojet 2.5KS-18000 booster, which
// burns 2.5 s. Built by hand from plain parts. The sustainer lights with the booster (the
// real one lit a second after launch, while the booster still burned), firing through the
// vented adapter it stands on, so its propellant never floats; the booster falls away with
// the adapter once it burns out.
